# Monthly table maintenance review memo

Audit date: 2026-09-01. The audit computes size class from `total_pages` (>=500 large, <500 small), computes bloat ratio as `dead_pages / total_pages` with round-half-up to 2 decimal places, and applies finding precedence autovacuum, bloat, stale.

## Non-compliant findings

- T-13 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because autovacuum is disabled, which overrides the bloat check even though total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 50 days (not legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.50 would face the stale tightened cap 0.15.
- T-17 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because autovacuum is disabled, overriding the bloat check even though total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 50 days (not legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.40 would face the tightened cap 0.15.
- T-27 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 46 days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.38 is over the tightened cap 0.15.
- T-04 is STALE_STATISTICS because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual date math gives 45 stale days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.10 is under the tightened cap 0.15.
- T-21 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because manual vacuum overrides autovacuum, even though total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 45 days, and ratio 0.20 would be over the tightened cap 0.15.
- T-26 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 36 days (not legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.18 is over the tightened cap 0.15.
- T-30 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 36 days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.20 is over the tightened cap 0.15.
- T-36 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 35 days (not the legacy days_since_analyze field), and ratio 0.18 is over the tightened cap 0.15.
- T-40 is STALE_STATISTICS because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual date math gives 35 stale days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.05 is under the tightened cap 0.15.
- T-42 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 35 days (not legacy days_since_analyze), and ratio 0.20 is over the tightened cap 0.15.
- T-45 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, actual staleness is 33 days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and round-half-up makes 155/1000 ratio 0.16, which is over the tightened cap 0.15.
- T-10 is STALE_STATISTICS because total_pages 1000 computes to large, stats are stale at 31 days (ignoring legacy days_since_analyze), and its approved active reindex is still valid through 2026-09-15, so ratio 0.21 is exempt from the bloat cap 0.15.
- T-16 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, stats are stale at 31 days, its reindex approval expired on 2026-08-25, and ratio 0.20 is over the tightened cap 0.15.
- T-19 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because total_pages 1000 computes to large, round-half-up makes 405/1000 ratio 0.41, which is over the cap 0.2.
